  "authoringNote": "Migrated from F02; expectations re-derived under pack v2. No order of any kind and no receipt record is supplied (stated in the scenario). R01 passes: scope facts and the named supplier record are explicit and supported; with no current usable order there is no order code to compare or cite, so it cites the seven supplier fields only. R02 passes and cites the encounter name and identifier. R03 is missing with R03.no_usable_order: no current usable order exists and no current, non-quarantined order is restricted, unreadable or failed provenance, so no candidate explains the gap (C09). R04 is missing with R04.no_usable_order for the same reason; the final encounter is usable, so R04 still cites its status, date and practitioner identifier (three) and no encounter condition holds. R05 is missing with R05.no_usable_receipt: no usable receipt and no receipt candidate exists. R05.no_usable_order does not hold because it requires at least one current usable receipt. All three missing conditions route to the authorization coordinator with effect needs_information and name no document; parent sets are empty (no restricted, unreadable or failed-provenance condition). R06 cites the five clinical statements; R07 passes citing the false LCMP flag; R08 and R09 pass. State needs_information, as in v1; v2 adds the three explicit condition tuples. No order is generated or drafted.",
